# Defect 456, 2026-10-07. Symptom: `heroes check` stopped with *panic:
# array index out of range*, exit 134, on a function head whose parameter
# type opens a `(` and closes it on the line below, the three lines below;
# `heroes probe`'s `paren` family writes the shape into two comments
# fixtures, which is where it was found. Cause: past the head's failed
# line, the search for a closer one too many stepped over a run of stray
# closers by place alone, and the view of a body lays its `dedent` and
# `eof` at its closing token's place, so the step went past the last token
# (`parse/brace_habit.a_closer_too_many`). It steps over the run's own
# closers now. The messages are the recovery's as it stands.

function f(a: (  #~v expected_function_type
        bool), b: bool)
    print(1)

# Moved 2026-10-09 with defect 496's repair (lane b15-parse): the line
# below a type broken after its `(` is the head's own, no body a closer one
# too many spilled into it (`spill_reading`), so the head is read to its
# end and each broken type is told once, its body read as the body; the
# reports past the type, `expected_end_of_line`, `expected_binding_symbol`
